          "snippet": "By way of a comparison, the optical tweezers were also used to controllably release particles from known x,y,z positions within the acoustic field. 5,22,23 The particles' subsequent motion to the centre of the acoustic trap were monitored and their velocity equated to the Stokes' drag on a sphere, a technique commonly known as Particle Image Velocimetry (PIV). 23 This allowed us to test the equivalence of the techniques and the repeatability and validity of PIV.",
