          "snippet": "For our purposes, we assume that the polymer tether is dsDNA, although our analysis remains applicable for other choices of tether molecules. In the limit of small displacements, we treat the DNA as a linear spring with constant k DNA ( eq ) ϭ dF DNA ͞d  eq , where we expand its force-extension behavior (22)(23)(24) about the equilibrium extension eq . The drag coefficient of each microsphere of radius r 1,2 , in the absence of the other microsphere, is given by ␥ 1,2 ϭ 6 r 1,2 , where is the viscosity of the solvent (9 ϫ 10 Ϫ10 pNs͞nm 2 for water).",
